Changes in version 1.15.1 (2026-10-14):

+ cellBody = "discModel" and cell body markers work again for several images
  of the same size, and cell body markers work for a single image.
+ An image where no nuclei pass the threshold gives a warning and an empty
  mask instead of an lm.fit error (#20).
+ simpleSeg() checks that nucleus and tissue markers exist, and checks
  watershed, cellBody and cores; nucleus can be given as channel positions.
+ normalizeCells() stops when imageID is missing and a per-image method is
  requested (#16, #22), and works with a single marker.
+ Faster segmentation with lower memory use: each image is processed once in
  one task, on plain arrays, with fitted values from one QR fit. Masks are
  unchanged.
+ Parallel processing starts the BiocParallel workers once per call, runs
  BLAS with one thread per worker, and gives every image its own random
  number stream, so masks do not depend on the number of cores.
+ terra, spatstat.geom and grDevices are no longer imported.
